and a place to sleep.

1287
00:53:15.781 --> 00:53:18.870
I had no commitments,

1288
00:53:18.870 --> 00:53:22.450
but I knew there was a Krishna temple in Vrindaban, India,

1289
00:53:22.450 --> 00:53:24.050
Holy place in India.

1290
00:53:24.050 --> 00:53:29.050
And I met some monks who were visiting America

1291
00:53:29.310 --> 00:53:30.510
and they invited me.

1292
00:53:30.510 --> 00:53:32.540
They say, if you wanna stop by in our ashram, while you go

1293
00:53:32.540 --> 00:53:35.130
through India, I knew I was going to India after my tour.

1294
00:53:35.130 --> 00:53:37.250
And it happened when I got back from tour

1295
00:53:37.250 --> 00:53:41.430
my father left his body and I was booked a ticket.

1296
00:53:41.430 --> 00:53:44.120
And I just left and realized like, all right

1297
00:53:44.120 --> 00:53:45.740
this is my path now.

1298
00:53:45.740 --> 00:53:47.550
And you got to the ashram and then--

1299
00:53:47.550 --> 00:53:48.383
I got to the ashram and you know--

1300
00:53:48.383 --> 00:53:50.160
That was your home for a while?

1301
00:53:50.160 --> 00:53:50.993
Yeah.

1302
00:53:53.800 --> 00:53:56.230
I had some money saved from touring,

1303
00:53:56.230 --> 00:53:58.700
not tons of money but I had like 25,000 bucks

1304
00:53:58.700 --> 00:54:00.410
and I was real, you know, I'm a New Yorker.

1305
00:54:00.410 --> 00:54:02.150
So I'm cynical of everything.

1306
00:54:02.150 --> 00:54:03.920
And I'm figuring like the monks are gonna try

1307
00:54:03.920 --> 00:54:05.220
to take my money probably.

1308
00:54:06.877 --> 00:54:08.280
It's all a scam.

1309
00:54:08.280 --> 00:54:10.190
It's all a scam guys.

1310
00:54:10.190 --> 00:54:11.587
But when you see how they live,

1311
00:54:11.587 --> 00:54:15.030
and India is a tough place to live, especially back then

1312
00:54:15.030 --> 00:54:16.030
there was no hot water.

1313
00:54:16.030 --> 00:54:19.550
It was like a jail house showers.

1314
00:54:19.550 --> 00:54:21.660
And it was cold in the winter.

1315
00:54:21.660 --> 00:54:24.010
It was cold and in the summer it was hot.

1316
00:54:24.010 --> 00:54:26.307
And there was no nothing was comfortable.

1317
00:54:26.307 --> 00:54:27.760
And there was no comfort.

1318
00:54:27.760 --> 00:54:29.710
Anything. There was no Netflix

1319
00:54:29.710 --> 00:54:32.630
or there was no like, you know, what did we do for comfort?

1320
00:54:32.630 --> 00:54:33.770
We shop, we have sex.

1321
00:54:33.770 --> 00:54:35.640
We, you know, we go out to dinner

1322
00:54:35.640 --> 00:54:37.300
we watch movies that you couldn't do any of that.

1323
00:54:37.300 --> 00:54:40.620
You're a monk, there's nothing to buy.

1324
00:54:40.620 --> 00:54:41.803
There's no shopping.

1325
00:54:44.170 --> 00:54:48.670
But I started being shocked about how happy the monks were.

1326
00:54:48.670 --> 00:54:53.060
I started thinking, man, what makes these guys tick?

1327
00:54:53.060 --> 00:54:55.530
Like, how can they be so happy with nothing?

1328
00:54:55.530 --> 00:54:58.960
They've given up everything, but you've probably experienced

1329
00:54:58.960 --> 00:55:00.820
that when you've like cleaned out your garage

1330
00:55:00.820 --> 00:55:03.890
and you're like, you feel free from the clutter of life.

1331
00:55:03.890 --> 00:55:04.723
And that's it.

1332
00:55:06.113 --> 00:55:09.700
I felt like God, if I can just learn what these guys have

1333
00:55:09.700 --> 00:55:11.286
my life could be successful.

1334
00:55:11.286 --> 00:55:15.010
How can you be joyful with nothing?

1335
00:55:15.010 --> 00:55:17.290
So it's not the things that are giving me joy.

1336
00:55:17.290 --> 00:55:19.810
I'm not going out there for my joy.

1337
00:55:19.810 --> 00:55:23.285
The joy has to come from something inside of me.

1338
00:55:23.285 --> 00:55:26.390
And that was like a beautiful thing to observe when you,

1339
00:55:26.390 --> 00:55:29.240
cause it's not a happy, it's not a fun.

1340
00:55:29.240 --> 00:55:30.830
They're not having fun.

1341
00:55:30.830 --> 00:55:33.843
They're just experiencing a joy from living.

1342
00:55:34.760 --> 00:55:36.260
And it's not based on their watch

1343
00:55:36.260 --> 00:55:39.390
or their outfit or what they're driving.

1344
00:55:39.390 --> 00:55:42.200
It's based on like an integrity of existence

1345
00:55:42.200 --> 00:55:44.450
and the way they treat each other and the way

1346
00:55:44.450 --> 00:55:47.400
and also the thoughts that are in your mind

1347
00:55:47.400 --> 00:55:49.160
what you're thinking on a regular basis.

1348
00:55:49.160 --> 00:55:51.540
Cause I realize a lot of my pain is from my mind

1349
00:55:51.540 --> 00:55:53.720
or my anguish or my envy for someone else

1350
00:55:53.720 --> 00:55:58.310
or some hate we might have for somebody for no good reason.

1351
00:55:58.310 --> 00:56:00.284
You know, you see somebody who's that idiot,

1352
00:56:00.284 --> 00:56:01.320
who's that idiot?

1353
00:56:01.320 --> 00:56:03.213
But why is my mind thinking like that?

1354
00:56:03.213 --> 00:56:04.380
Like the guy's an idiot.

1355
00:56:04.380 --> 00:56:06.100
I don't even know that person.

1356
00:56:06.100 --> 00:56:07.340
So what is the process

1357
00:56:07.340 --> 00:56:10.440
of rewiring that like when you go to the ashram

1358
00:56:10.440 --> 00:56:14.440
and you start living as a monk, what is the teaching like?

1359
00:56:14.440 --> 00:56:18.660
And what is the day-to-day existence where you start to

1360
00:56:19.550 --> 00:56:24.040
you know, intuit these teachings and put them into practice?

1361
00:56:24.040 --> 00:56:27.700
Well, there's a lot to share.

1362
00:56:27.700 --> 00:56:30.810
I'm working on a book right now that extracted six

1363
00:56:30.810 --> 00:56:34.398
very powerful principles that I taught from the teachings.

1364
00:56:34.398 --> 00:56:38.530
And the first one is, and these are based on the teachings

1365
00:56:38.530 --> 00:56:41.503
of Chaitanya Mahaprabhu who is a great,

1366
00:56:44.450 --> 00:56:47.530
considered by some as a child prodigy,

1367
00:56:47.530 --> 00:56:50.730
cause he was a child prodigy in Sanskrit.

1368
00:56:50.730 --> 00:56:53.090
Some other people that knew more intimately thought of

1369
00:56:53.090 --> 00:56:55.190
he was a mystic cause he did, he performed

1370
00:56:55.190 --> 00:56:58.350
so many mystical things, Christ-like mysticism.

1371
00:56:58.350 --> 00:57:01.700
And then, but his intimate followers who are great

1372
00:57:01.700 --> 00:57:03.310
gurus in their own, right.

1373
00:57:03.310 --> 00:57:04.730
They considered him an avatar.

1374
00:57:04.730 --> 00:57:07.330
So his teachings were very simple

1375
00:57:07.330 --> 00:57:10.220
and one of them is very basic.

1376
00:57:10.220 --> 00:57:11.830
And it's a great takeaway.

1377
00:57:11.830 --> 00:57:13.525
If you wanna take away anything from today,

1378
00:57:13.525 --> 00:57:15.090
you can take this way.

1379
00:57:15.090 --> 00:57:17.420
Stop criticizing other people

1380
00:57:18.660 --> 00:57:23.660
Like the sound coming out of your mouth can be toxic.

1381
00:57:27.110 --> 00:57:28.870
And that was a powerful thing.

1382
00:57:28.870 --> 00:57:29.850
Stop criticizing.

1383
00:57:29.850 --> 00:57:33.180
I realized I'm living with so much criticism in my mind.

1384
00:57:33.180 --> 00:57:35.280
That doesn't mean we should throw discernment out.

1385
00:57:35.280 --> 00:57:36.550
We need discernment.

1386
00:57:36.550 --> 00:57:39.210
But the condemning language that happens

1387
00:57:39.210 --> 00:57:42.210
on a regular basis from finding fault with other people

1388
00:57:42.210 --> 00:57:45.240
and how you would do things so much better.

1389
00:57:45.240 --> 00:57:47.390
If you were doing them, cut it out.

1390
00:57:47.390 --> 00:57:49.410
Stop letting that pour out of your mouth.

1391
00:57:49.410 --> 00:57:50.303
That's a big one.

1392
00:57:52.930 --> 00:57:54.220
If you want, I'll just run through these--

1393
00:57:54.220 --> 00:57:55.053
Yeah let's do it.

1394
00:57:55.053 --> 00:57:55.886
No, this is great.

1395
00:57:55.886 --> 00:57:58.093
And first of all, when did this guy live?

1396
00:57:59.110 --> 00:58:02.520
1400, the same time Columbus was showing up here.

1397
00:58:02.520 --> 00:58:05.920
This person Chaitanya Mahaprabhu was

1398
00:58:05.920 --> 00:58:09.220
in Bengal and traveled throughout India and Korea.

1399
00:58:09.220 --> 00:58:11.977
And basically it was a Renaissance of Bhakti.

1400
00:58:11.977 --> 00:58:14.020
Bhakti means.

1401
00:58:14.020 --> 00:58:18.560
Bhakti Yoga means connecting to source through love.

1402
00:58:18.560 --> 00:58:20.820
That's all the word really means.

1403
00:58:20.820 --> 00:58:25.290
And so a lot of the practices, our singing, our cooking

1404
00:58:25.290 --> 00:58:29.680
our meditation, but everything is an action, right?

1405
00:58:29.680 --> 00:58:33.560
You're acting in a loving way and dealing with other people.

1406
00:58:33.560 --> 00:58:37.900
And so yeah, this is one of the teachings I call it.

1407
00:58:37.900 --> 00:58:41.026
The book is called the Six Pillars of Bhakti.

1408
00:58:41.026 --> 00:58:43.730
And so one is not criticizing.

1409
00:58:43.730 --> 00:58:45.170
The second one is being tolerant.

1410
00:58:45.170 --> 00:58:47.730
Whereas criticism deals with other people

1411
00:58:47.730 --> 00:58:51.440
and other one is just dealing with life situation

1412
00:58:51.440 --> 00:58:54.840
and stop blaming the world for your own happiness.

1413
00:58:54.840 --> 00:58:56.230
And this is very powerful.

1414
00:58:56.230 --> 00:58:57.590
It's transformational.

1415
00:58:57.590 --> 00:58:58.870
Even if you're a materialist,

1416
00:58:58.870 --> 00:59:01.490
this main teaching can transform your life.

1417
00:59:01.490 --> 00:59:02.770
But if you wanna really experience

1418
00:59:02.770 --> 00:59:05.070
like the higher echelons of meditation

1419
00:59:05.070 --> 00:59:09.680
it's gotta be there, criticism, tolerance.

1420
00:59:09.680 --> 00:59:11.210
And this is a huge one.

1421
00:59:11.210 --> 00:59:12.273
That number three.

1422
00:59:13.390 --> 00:59:16.310
If you can add this one to your life,

1423
00:59:16.310 --> 00:59:17.450
it's a such a game changer.

1424
00:59:17.450 --> 00:59:21.730
It's I take no offense,

1425
00:59:21.730 --> 00:59:25.800
meaning I will not be offended on a regular basis.

1426
00:59:25.800 --> 00:59:26.840
And that's a very common thing.

1427
00:59:26.840 --> 00:59:29.077
Sometimes we could see somebody talking over there

1428
00:59:29.077 --> 00:59:30.100
and I get offended.

1429
00:59:30.100 --> 00:59:31.500
I think they're talking about me.

1430
00:59:31.500 --> 00:59:33.070
So without provocation,

1431
00:59:33.070 --> 00:59:36.910
I think someone's got something against me.

1432
00:59:36.910 --> 00:59:40.780
And sometimes we'll walk around holding some resentment

1433
00:59:43.060 --> 00:59:46.053
for a person who didn't even mean anything.

1434
00:59:46.053 --> 00:59:49.430
And that gets split in two things,

1435
00:59:49.430 --> 00:59:51.630
cause sometimes people don't mean anything, but due to my

1436
00:59:51.630 --> 00:59:55.010
some proclivity that I have, that I don't trust the world

1437
00:59:55.010 --> 00:59:57.850
that I take an offense and I carry that resentment

1438
00:59:57.850 --> 01:00:00.520
around with me and it becomes a burden

1439
01:00:00.520 --> 01:00:03.010
but sometimes people have hurt me.

1440
01:00:03.010 --> 01:00:07.280
They've actually deliberately hurt me, but still that desire

1441
01:00:07.280 --> 01:00:09.773
or that need to forgive has to be there,

1442
01:00:10.670 --> 01:00:13.170
because in the Bhakti culture

1443
01:00:13.170 --> 01:00:16.610
is nothing's actually happening to me it's happening for me.

1444
01:00:16.610 --> 01:00:20.330
That there is a benevolent energy lifting us higher

1445
01:00:20.330 --> 01:00:21.790
and higher and higher.

1446
01:00:21.790 --> 01:00:26.110
And we have to see that everything is for my edification

1447
01:00:26.110 --> 01:00:30.000
for my purification and sometimes even tragic things.

1448
01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:33.040
And so there's a firm faith that everything's happening

1449
01:00:33.040 --> 01:00:37.960
for me and that we shouldn't be heartless when it comes

1450
01:00:37.960 --> 01:00:40.130
to someone else's suffering, I should see,

1451
01:00:40.130 --> 01:00:41.710
he's having a hard time.

1452
01:00:41.710 --> 01:00:43.680
We should feel like I have to reach out to that person.

1453
01:00:43.680 --> 01:00:44.880
They're having a hard time.

1454
01:00:44.880 --> 01:00:47.470
But for my own situation, I should feel like,

1455
01:00:47.470 --> 01:00:50.020
I'm going through a hard time

1456
01:00:50.020 --> 01:00:52.860
and this must be for my benefit.

1457
01:00:52.860 --> 01:00:54.510
What is that benefit?

1458
01:00:54.510 --> 01:00:56.750
And I can look at life like that.

1459
01:00:56.750 --> 01:00:58.570
So we don't hold any resentment.

1460
01:00:58.570 --> 01:01:00.463
We don't criticize, we're tolerant.

1461
01:01:01.830 --> 01:01:05.070
Next one, we see the good in others and we let them know it.

1462
01:01:05.070 --> 01:01:07.200
Find good and this is where we're talking about instead

1463
01:01:07.200 --> 01:01:10.450
of finding what this person is doing so wrong.

1464
01:01:10.450 --> 01:01:12.180
What are they doing right?

1465
01:01:12.180 --> 01:01:13.230
Why are they good?

1466
01:01:13.230 --> 01:01:16.230
This is such a powerful practice in this day and age,

1467
01:01:16.230 --> 01:01:18.310
because otherwise we're gonna lock in

1468
01:01:18.310 --> 01:01:22.170
and we're just gonna foster hate with others.

1469
01:01:22.170 --> 01:01:24.370
And we're gonna have no commonality whatsoever.

1470
01:01:24.370 --> 01:01:25.640
What do we have in common?

1471
01:01:25.640 --> 01:01:27.500
What is right about this person?

1472
01:01:27.500 --> 01:01:29.130
And it's such a great thing, truthfully,

1473
01:01:29.130 --> 01:01:30.700
it's a marriage saver.

1474
01:01:30.700 --> 01:01:32.490
It's a relationship saver.

1475
01:01:32.490 --> 01:01:35.760
You know, what is good about this person?

1476
01:01:35.760 --> 01:01:36.630
And then sharing it with them,

1477
01:01:36.630 --> 01:01:39.060
tell him why I appreciate you.

1478
01:01:39.060 --> 01:01:42.363
And that lack of appreciation can really kill.

1479
01:01:43.920 --> 01:01:46.010
It can kill love quick.

1480
01:01:46.010 --> 01:01:49.610
I mean, isn't that what romance is full 100% appreciation

1481
01:01:49.610 --> 01:01:50.443
for that person

1482
01:01:50.443 --> 01:01:55.443
And the second piece about letting that person know

1483
01:01:55.800 --> 01:01:58.688
is crazy, powerful.

1484
01:01:58.688 --> 01:02:00.430
And it's something that most

1485
01:02:00.430 --> 01:02:02.790
of us don't do nearly enough of.

1486
01:02:02.790 --> 01:02:04.020
I mean we might have a person

1487
01:02:04.020 --> 01:02:06.000
that would do anything for us.

1488
01:02:06.000 --> 01:02:09.467
They would come anywhere at any time at any moment,

1489
01:02:09.467 --> 01:02:10.610
"Hey, I need your help.

1490
01:02:10.610 --> 01:02:11.609
Can you come here?

1491
01:02:11.609 --> 01:02:14.290
That person I never let them know

1492
01:02:14.290 --> 01:02:15.610
how much I appreciate them.

1493
01:02:15.610 --> 01:02:17.800
Sometimes the people that are the closest to us

1494
01:02:17.800 --> 01:02:20.945
we never share with them how we appreciate them.

1495
01:02:20.945 --> 01:02:23.280
And then you recounting these lessons.

1496
01:02:23.280 --> 01:02:25.930
I'm thinking this should be the terms

1497
01:02:25.930 --> 01:02:27.290
and conditions on Twitter.

1498
01:02:27.290 --> 01:02:29.630
Like what if you, before you could log on to Twitter

1499
01:02:29.630 --> 01:02:33.193
you had to read through these sort of guidelines,

1500
01:02:35.070 --> 01:02:35.950
sort of guideposts

1501
01:02:35.950 --> 01:02:37.900
for how to behave or acquit yourself.

1502
01:02:37.900 --> 01:02:42.820
Because everything that you just shared is so anathema

1503
01:02:42.820 --> 01:02:46.080
to the way that we conduct ourselves in the kind

1504
01:02:46.080 --> 01:02:49.100
of public conversations that are happening on social media.

1505
01:02:49.100 --> 01:02:52.440
And we're all seeing, the fractures,

1506
01:02:52.440 --> 01:02:57.440
the fissures that are starting to expand in the fabric

1507
01:02:58.080 --> 01:03:00.410
of our society.

1508
01:03:00.410 --> 01:03:04.730
Like we're no longer able to productively communicate

1509
01:03:04.730 --> 01:03:05.690
in a healthy way.

1510
01:03:05.690 --> 01:03:09.470
And it's because we've lost sight of these very things

1511
01:03:09.470 --> 01:03:14.470
that allow us to remember that we are truly one.

1512
01:03:16.120 --> 01:03:17.170
And no one's happy.

1513
01:03:18.040 --> 01:03:18.910
They're all sad.

1514
01:03:18.910 --> 01:03:20.270
Even if they're righteous, they're just

1515
01:03:20.270 --> 01:03:23.993
like sad in their righteousness or their rightness.

1516
01:03:27.400 --> 01:03:32.300
So anyway, that's see the good in others, let them know it.

1517
01:03:32.300 --> 01:03:34.800
The appreciation is such a powerful,

1518
01:03:34.800 --> 01:03:36.577
it's powerful in this world

1519
01:03:36.577 --> 01:03:39.130
and it's powerful in the spiritual realm as well.

1520
01:03:39.130 --> 01:03:42.309
That's why I love this stuff because it's relevant.

1521
01:03:42.309 --> 01:03:43.142
It's real.

1522
01:03:43.142 --> 01:03:46.010
It's not just like when I die, I'll go to heaven.

1523
01:03:46.010 --> 01:03:46.870
Who cares?

1524
01:03:46.870 --> 01:03:47.830
I don't know about heaven.

1525
01:03:47.830 --> 01:03:48.900
I don't know anything about heaven.

1526
01:03:48.900 --> 01:03:50.430
I don't even know if it's real,

1527
01:03:50.430 --> 01:03:53.490
