2366
01:40:50.550 --> 01:40:52.950
He just says, I got a gun

2367
01:40:54.620 --> 01:40:56.453
And I'm gonna kill everyone tonight.

2368
01:40:58.510 --> 01:41:01.310
It was like one of these moments in your life where like

2369
01:41:02.220 --> 01:41:04.700
okay, tonight's the night we're gonna die tonight.

2370
01:41:04.700 --> 01:41:06.380
It wasn't like run for your life.

2371
01:41:06.380 --> 01:41:07.410
Let's fight back.

2372
01:41:07.410 --> 01:41:10.750
Let's it's like, tonight's, we're gonna die.

2373
01:41:10.750 --> 01:41:12.960
And I was sort of like the older one.

2374
01:41:12.960 --> 01:41:14.780
And I had, you know, all the other monks that were

2375
01:41:14.780 --> 01:41:17.400
with me were a little younger than me.

2376
01:41:17.400 --> 01:41:18.450
So everybody gathered around me,

2377
01:41:18.450 --> 01:41:20.910
like rocking off what are we gonna do?

2378
01:41:20.910 --> 01:41:25.577
And to me, it was just like, we're gonna die.

2379
01:41:25.577 --> 01:41:26.410
What do you mean?

2380
01:41:26.410 --> 01:41:27.243
What are we gonna do?

2381
01:41:27.243 --> 01:41:28.076
We're gonna die.

2382
01:41:28.076 --> 01:41:30.120
So you know what we're gonna do we're gonna chant.

2383
01:41:30.120 --> 01:41:31.550
I don't know where that came from.

2384
01:41:31.550 --> 01:41:34.440
I'm not a spiritually evolved being,

2385
01:41:34.440 --> 01:41:36.160
if you get to hang out with me long enough,

2386
01:41:36.160 --> 01:41:37.930
you'll realize that.

2387
01:41:37.930 --> 01:41:38.950
But for some reason.

2388
01:41:38.950 --> 01:41:40.080
There's nothing else to do.

2389
01:41:40.080 --> 01:41:44.600
Was this before or during your MMA?

2390
01:41:44.600 --> 01:41:46.520
Before, much before.

2391
01:41:46.520 --> 01:41:48.160
This was me--
Maybe this motivated you.

2392
01:41:48.160 --> 01:41:50.133
Eating lots of Indian sweets.

2393
01:41:51.132 --> 01:41:53.800
(indistinct)

2394
01:41:53.800 --> 01:41:55.210
MMA made my way out of this one though.

2395
01:41:55.210 --> 01:41:57.460
It was one of those things, massive man

2396
01:41:57.460 --> 01:41:59.260
with a gang of other massive people

2397
01:41:59.260 --> 01:42:01.590
with weapons I wasn't gonna get out of this one.

2398
01:42:01.590 --> 01:42:05.570
So I just, I just thought we're gonna die right now.

2399
01:42:05.570 --> 01:42:07.500
And it was one of those you ever had one

2400
01:42:07.500 --> 01:42:09.090
of those experiences where you gonna die?

2401
01:42:09.090 --> 01:42:10.980
That felt like they were gonna die right now.

2402
01:42:10.980 --> 01:42:15.980
So I went in and I got a clay Indian drum, which I play.

2403
01:42:16.970 --> 01:42:20.480
And I started chanting these mantras.

2404
01:42:20.480 --> 01:42:21.900
These (indistinct) mantras

2405
01:42:21.900 --> 01:42:24.530
these prayers to Lord Vishnu as the protector.

2406
01:42:24.530 --> 01:42:25.890
And we all gathered a circle.

2407
01:42:25.890 --> 01:42:28.810
It was incredibly surreal rich,

2408
01:42:28.810 --> 01:42:32.630
we're in a circle chanting these mantras

2409
01:42:32.630 --> 01:42:35.110
while these guys are going around the club

2410
01:42:35.110 --> 01:42:36.493
just demolishing people.

2411
01:42:37.625 --> 01:42:38.458
I don't know what people say.

2412
01:42:38.458 --> 01:42:39.291
Well, why didn't you run?

2413
01:42:39.291 --> 01:42:40.230
I don't know.

2414
01:42:40.230 --> 01:42:43.210
I don't know what was going on

2415
01:42:43.210 --> 01:42:44.330
but we all started chanting.

2416
01:42:44.330 --> 01:42:47.470
And then they all started coming towards us.

2417
01:42:47.470 --> 01:42:49.630
And all my guys ran,

2418
01:42:49.630 --> 01:42:52.300
some guys ran under the van, in the van, over the van.

2419
01:42:52.300 --> 01:42:54.060
It was just like, everybody's scattered.

2420
01:42:54.060 --> 01:42:59.060
And I was surrounded by these people, holding the drum.

2421
01:42:59.230 --> 01:43:00.810
And I didn't even know what to say.

2422
01:43:00.810 --> 01:43:02.903
So I just put my hands like in a namaste,

2423
01:43:04.200 --> 01:43:05.480
still holding this drum.

2424
01:43:05.480 --> 01:43:09.050
And I said, oh, the guy pulled out a gun.

2425
01:43:09.050 --> 01:43:11.153
And he said, "You want some.

2426
01:43:12.880 --> 01:43:14.460
I thought to myself, "Oh my God

2427
01:43:14.460 --> 01:43:15.650
how am I supposed to answer this?"

2428
01:43:15.650 --> 01:43:18.983
Do I want some, I said, Hare Krishna,

2429
01:43:20.890 --> 01:43:22.103
I'm a Krishna monk.

2430
01:43:23.070 --> 01:43:26.503
I have no idea why you guys are so angry.

2431
01:43:28.500 --> 01:43:33.500
And then I felt a barrage of fists coming to my face

2432
01:43:33.980 --> 01:43:37.710
and I've never, ever felt helpless in my life.

2433
01:43:37.710 --> 01:43:40.703
But at that time I felt like incredibly helpless.

2434
01:43:41.830 --> 01:43:46.830
And as I'm getting punched, I was just chanting, chanting

2435
01:43:49.440 --> 01:43:51.580
like different names of God.

2436
01:43:51.580 --> 01:43:54.400
Krishna, Rum, Govinda, Chaitanya, like this

2437
01:43:54.400 --> 01:43:56.190
just like running through my mind.

2438
01:43:56.190 --> 01:43:58.163
And as I'm getting pounded,

2439
01:43:59.595 --> 01:44:01.360
I'm starting to think of all these great stories.

2440
01:44:01.360 --> 01:44:04.471
I've studied the Maha-Bharata, the Ramayana,

2441
01:44:04.471 --> 01:44:06.610
(speaking in foreign language)

2442
01:44:06.610 --> 01:44:09.060
they're stories of sort of people

2443
01:44:09.060 --> 01:44:12.360
in destitute positions in their life and the

2444
01:44:12.360 --> 01:44:14.370
how they leave their bodies.

2445
01:44:14.370 --> 01:44:17.140
And they generally the auspicious way, the wonderful way

2446
01:44:17.140 --> 01:44:21.329
to leave their body is they focus their mind

2447
01:44:21.329 --> 01:44:24.910
on the supreme being on God, on your higher power.

2448
01:44:24.910 --> 01:44:26.600
They've had their focus

2449
01:44:26.600 --> 01:44:29.500
and they're just chanting these mantras.

2450
01:44:29.500 --> 01:44:32.400
And I'm thinking about these great personalities

2451
01:44:32.400 --> 01:44:36.700
in these great epics of India thinking, wow

2452
01:44:36.700 --> 01:44:40.610
all these people died like this, and now I'm gonna die.

2453
01:44:40.610 --> 01:44:43.853
And I'm also dying in the same way they are dying.

2454
01:44:45.090 --> 01:44:50.090
I am so fortunate and I can honestly say there was not fear

2455
01:44:50.270 --> 01:44:52.420
and there was not anger.

2456
01:44:52.420 --> 01:44:56.895
There was just a type of like great appreciation

2457
01:44:56.895 --> 01:44:59.350
for the way I'm gonna leave my body.

2458
01:44:59.350 --> 01:45:02.330
And it got worse because as I started getting beat up

2459
01:45:02.330 --> 01:45:06.190
I saw these women coming at me with baseball bats

2460
01:45:06.190 --> 01:45:08.200
and I thought they were coming to save me

2461
01:45:08.200 --> 01:45:10.630
but they were the girlfriends of these guys.

2462
01:45:10.630 --> 01:45:14.690
And they started pounding me with baseball bats

2463
01:45:14.690 --> 01:45:15.680
but the same thing too,

2464
01:45:15.680 --> 01:45:18.480
I was like chanting and chanting and chanting.

2465
01:45:18.480 --> 01:45:20.593
And it just all stopped.

2466
01:45:22.460 --> 01:45:24.910
And I didn't know what happened.

2467
01:45:24.910 --> 01:45:27.273
And I was covered in blood.

2468
01:45:28.130 --> 01:45:30.560
And what actually happened was the rest

2469
01:45:30.560 --> 01:45:34.900
of the band had jumped in our van and just started the van

2470
01:45:34.900 --> 01:45:38.450
and plowed through their car and escaped.

2471
01:45:38.450 --> 01:45:39.700
And when they did a head count

2472
01:45:39.700 --> 01:45:41.959
they didn't realize I wasn't in the van with them.

2473
01:45:41.959 --> 01:45:43.220
So I didn't know what was happening.

2474
01:45:43.220 --> 01:45:46.460
And I guess I was experiencing some type of, you know

2475
01:45:48.929 --> 01:45:51.148
Altered.
Altered state.

2476
01:45:51.148 --> 01:45:54.660
I was looking for the band basically.

2477
01:45:54.660 --> 01:45:58.160
And I was out in the streets looking through--

2478
01:45:58.160 --> 01:46:00.344
The attackers dispersed.

2479
01:46:00.344 --> 01:46:02.350
Yeah, I guess they dispersed.

2480
01:46:02.350 --> 01:46:04.150
And I went into the streets and I was trying

2481
01:46:04.150 --> 01:46:06.580
to flag down cars because I thought my band

2482
01:46:06.580 --> 01:46:09.260
was getting beat up or killed or something.

2483
01:46:09.260 --> 01:46:11.120
And every time a car would see me

2484
01:46:11.120 --> 01:46:12.840
they'd slow down and they'd look at me.

2485
01:46:12.840 --> 01:46:15.543
And I was ever see that movie,

2486
01:46:15.543 --> 01:46:17.820
Carrie when you were a teenager, like covered in blood

2487
01:46:17.820 --> 01:46:20.911
and I'm still holding this clay drum covered in blood.

2488
01:46:20.911 --> 01:46:23.910
I'm thinking like a Yogi John wick.

2489
01:46:23.910 --> 01:46:27.370
It must've been so creepy to see me.

2490
01:46:27.370 --> 01:46:29.240
And I wouldn't have stopped for me either

2491
01:46:29.240 --> 01:46:31.170
if I was driving through a ghetto,

2492
01:46:31.170 --> 01:46:33.210
but everyone just kept on stopping.

2493
01:46:33.210 --> 01:46:34.043
And I was like,

2494
01:46:34.043 --> 01:46:36.300
oh my God my whole band is about to get killed.

2495
01:46:36.300 --> 01:46:40.180
And I'm walking into,

2496
01:46:40.180 --> 01:46:42.690
I saw some light on, it must have been two

2497
01:46:42.690 --> 01:46:44.100
in the morning, somewhere in Buffalo.

2498
01:46:44.100 --> 01:46:47.530
And I saw some man in a booth, like in a bus station.

2499
01:46:47.530 --> 01:46:49.930
And I said, hey, you've got to call police.

2500
01:46:49.930 --> 01:46:52.060
My friends are in trouble.

2501
01:46:52.060 --> 01:46:55.117
And the guy looked at me and just said, "I'm busy."

2502
01:46:56.220 --> 01:46:59.310
And I was so like, shocked

2503
01:46:59.310 --> 01:47:04.310
about how little this guy cared about human tragedy.

2504
01:47:04.370 --> 01:47:07.550
And I said, you gotta call the police

2505
01:47:07.550 --> 01:47:09.630
or I'm gonna go in there and call the police.

2506
01:47:09.630 --> 01:47:12.140
Now, get away from your phone or give me the phone.

2507
01:47:12.140 --> 01:47:15.280
And I think this was before cell phones maybe

2508
01:47:15.280 --> 01:47:18.590
or maybe I'm not sure, I didn't have a cell phone.

2509
01:47:18.590 --> 01:47:21.250
So anyway, he said, "All right, I'll call the police.

2510
01:47:21.250 --> 01:47:23.170
And I said, "If you don't mind, I'm just gonna stay here.

2511
01:47:23.170 --> 01:47:26.420
Cause these guys might come back and kill me.

2512
01:47:26.420 --> 01:47:28.970
And so I realized at that point like,

2513
01:47:28.970 --> 01:47:32.930
oh my God my head's probably split open.

2514
01:47:32.930 --> 01:47:34.930
And this is how people die.

2515
01:47:34.930 --> 01:47:37.280
Their head cracks open, their brain swells.

2516
01:47:37.280 --> 01:47:38.350
And they fall asleep and die.

2517
01:47:38.350 --> 01:47:40.250
And I was like, oh crap.

2518
01:47:40.250 --> 01:47:42.010
I wasn't expecting to die tonight.

2519
01:47:42.010 --> 01:47:43.650
I have a whole tour plans.

2520
01:47:43.650 --> 01:47:47.960
I have like, I have so many plans and I'm gonna die tonight.

2521
01:47:47.960 --> 01:47:49.620
This wasn't the day.

2522
01:47:49.620 --> 01:47:53.200
But I guess this is what I always teach.

2523
01:47:53.200 --> 01:47:54.720
This is what the books always teach.

2524
01:47:54.720 --> 01:47:56.480
This is what the wisdom literature teaches

2525
01:47:56.480 --> 01:47:59.460
that you don't expect death to happen tonight.

2526
01:47:59.460 --> 01:48:02.863
It happens what appears to be randomly.

2527
01:48:03.960 --> 01:48:06.420
And for some reason, Raghu

2528
01:48:06.420 --> 01:48:09.060
I'm talking to myself for some reason, Raghu

2529
01:48:09.060 --> 01:48:14.060
you got blessed tonight to experience what it's like to die

2530
01:48:14.240 --> 01:48:15.960
in a wonderful way.

2531
01:48:15.960 --> 01:48:20.960
But now you're in sad shape because you've lived.

2532
01:48:20.980 --> 01:48:23.550
And if you've got this head trauma, I don't know much.

2533
01:48:23.550 --> 01:48:24.710
I'm not a doctor or anything.

2534
01:48:24.710 --> 01:48:26.690
But what I understand is your brain swells,

2535
01:48:26.690 --> 01:48:29.610
you fall asleep and then you die.

2536
01:48:29.610 --> 01:48:30.790
You get a concussion and you die.

2537
01:48:30.790 --> 01:48:34.310
So I was like, oh my God, my mom doesn't know I am here.

2538
01:48:34.310 --> 01:48:35.900
My friends don't know where I am.

2539
01:48:35.900 --> 01:48:38.180
I'm gonna die in this disgusting,

2540
01:48:38.180 --> 01:48:41.893
mechanic shop or bus terminal or wherever I am.

2541
01:48:42.740 --> 01:48:46.230
And I started praying, sincerely.

2542
01:48:46.230 --> 01:48:50.023
I said, Krishna God, you've been so kind to me.

2543
01:48:50.980 --> 01:48:55.010
You gave me this glimpse into what it's like to be evolved

2544
01:48:55.010 --> 01:48:56.783
even though I'm not evolved.

2545
01:49:00.110 --> 01:49:02.840
And now I'm gonna just die with a concussion, please.

2546
01:49:02.840 --> 01:49:05.660
If you want to take me, take me now.

2547
01:49:05.660 --> 01:49:08.140
And I started chanting these beautiful prayers

2548
01:49:08.140 --> 01:49:09.290
I had memorized, which we do.

2549
01:49:09.290 --> 01:49:10.123
Sometimes we're on tour.

2550
01:49:10.123 --> 01:49:11.750
